# Copy to .env and adjust. docker compose reads this file automatically.

# Leave EMPTY unless you know you need it. The proxy embeds its own address in
# the manifest URLs it hands back; empty means it uses the Host header of each
# request, which is by definition an address the client can reach. Set it only
# when the Host header is not what clients should use (e.g. behind a reverse
# proxy), in which case give the address clients must use, e.g. the LAN IP of
# this host: http://192.168.1.3:8002
PROXY_BASE_URL=

# lucida.to service used for search. qobuz works today; the fallback chain
# (qobuz, grilledcheese, soundcloud) covers a service lucida breaks upstream.
LUCIDA_SERVICE=qobuz

# Country used when fetching item pages and starting downloads. Leave EMPTY:
# that sends the literal "auto" and lets lucida pick the account, which is what
# it does anyway. Search does not use this - each service accepts a different
# set, and the proxy discovers that set from lucida's own response rather than
# hardcoding it (see README, "Search countries are discovered, not hardcoded").
LUCIDA_COUNTRY=
